old text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The defense-shred window is the whole hero\"]}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Saber is not a flashy combo assassin. He is a timing window.\"}]\n80:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Everything in his kit is there to make Triple Sweep hit a target that has already been softened, slowed, and cornered. Enemy's Bane strips physical defense over repeated contact. Orbiting Swords gives you the repeated contact. Charge gives you the angle fix and the slow that keeps the victim in front of you. Triple Sweep is just the part everyone notices because it lifts the target into the air.\"}]\n81:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"This is why strong Saber players do not open fights by panic-ulting the first low-HP bar they see. They want Orbiting Swords active before the commit, because the swords give the engage real weight and every follow-up basic attack sends another blade into the target. Those extra contacts matter twice: they raise your burst and they shorten the wait for the second Charge, which is often the only reason you live after the kill.\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Think of Saber less like a diver and more like a receipt printer. Once the target is tagged, the rest of the combo is mostly paperwork. If you skip the setup and press Triple Sweep raw, you are cashing out the crowd control before the hero has earned his damage.\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Jungle: the first four minutes\"]}]\n84:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Take Orbiting Swords first and max it before Charge.\"}],\" Saber's first skill is clear speed, passive setup, and post-engage mobility all in one button. Start with S1, let it do the camp work, and keep your early path tidy instead of burning Charge for style points.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Your first real gank starts at level 4, not earlier.\"}],\" Before Triple Sweep, Saber is mostly chip damage plus a dash. After level 4, he becomes a guaranteed pick threat on any lane that is pushed too far or missing instant peel. Approach from the side bush, activate S1 before vision, and hold Charge until you know which direction the target wants to leave.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Save Retribution for tempo that matters.\"}],\" Spending it to clear one camp half a second faster is lazy. Save it for a contested buff, the first Turtle setup, or a lane gank where the slow secures a kill your normal combo would not. Saber snowballs through clean sequences, not through rushed clears.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The first four minutes are not about farming faster than a utility jungler. They are about arriving on time to one side lane with level 4 and punishing the first disrespectful wave state. If you leave the opening with one kill, one objective, and no unnecessary death, Saber is on schedule.\"}]\n86:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Hunter Strike plus Heptaseas is the first real kill window\"]}]\n87:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"Sabers that feel useless usually have not hit the right item pair yet. The first real spike is \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Hunter Strike plus Blade of the Heptaseas\"}],\", usually around the 7 to 9 minute mark in a stable game.\"]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Blade of the Heptaseas changes the opening touch. If you enter from fog after staying out of damage, your first basic attack hits harder and slows the target. That matters because Saber does not want to spend Charge just to begin the fight. He wants the opener to come from the brush, force the enemy to panic, then use Charge only after the target has committed to the wrong escape line.\"}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Hunter Strike changes the exit. Saber strings together enough consecutive hits to trigger its movement burst in real fights, which means your one-target pick suddenly includes a way out. Before this two-item window, a kill often feels like a trade. After it, you can delete a carry and still slide back toward the wall before the peel arrives.\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-12\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"This spike does not turn Saber into a tank killer. It turns him into a reliable first-contact assassin. Once you have both items, you stop asking whether the combo can kill a normal squishy and start asking whether the enemy has the tools to stop you from reaching them in the first place. That is a much better problem to have.\"}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"$La5\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n8c:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Teamfights: flank, lock, leave\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The wrong Saber reflex is to press Triple Sweep on the first enemy who steps into range. If that enemy is the tank, you just traded your entire hero for a crowd-control animation.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Wait until peel shows itself.\"}],\" Do not be the first body in. Let Khufra bounce, let Franco reveal the hook angle, let Chou spend Shunpo, let Akai commit the spin. Saber gets cleaner kills when the anti-dive tools are already pointed somewhere else.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Approach from the side, not through the front.\"}],\" You are not trying to prove you can cross a tank line. You are trying to make the enemy carry turn their camera too late. If your path starts by touching the enemy frontliner, the flank is already bad.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Hero-lock before you Charge.\"}],\" Saber is one of the most target-sensitive assassins in the game. Wrong target means no second chance. Set the lock first, then commit, then leave the moment the job is done.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"One support edge case changes the rule: if your roamer is Mathilda, you can take deeper entries than normal because the exit is more forgiving. Without that kind of rescue, play Saber like a rented car. Use him hard for one turn, then hand him back immediately.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Itemization is three locked burst pieces plus real flex slots\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Treat Saber as three locked burst pieces and several actual conversations.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"The locked burst pieces are \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"jungle boots, Hunter Strike, and Blade of the Heptaseas\"}],\". Those are the items that make the hero feel like Saber instead of a weaker physical assassin. Hunter Strike gives the damage and post-combo movement. Heptaseas gives the real fog-of-war opener. Without both, too many picks turn into half-kills.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"The boot conversation is simple. \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Warrior Boots\"}],\" are for heavy physical burst where surviving the counter-hit matters more than squeezing damage. \",\"$La6\",\" are for drafts loaded with control where one shorter stun is the difference between leaving and feeding.\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$La7\",\"\\n\",\"$La8\",\"\\n\",\"$La9\",\"\\n\",\"$Laa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lab\",\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb2\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb3\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb4\"]\n8d:[\"$\",\"$Lb5\",null,{\"heroName\":\"Saber\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8e:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidden card-hover hover:border-mlbb-gold/50\",\"style\":{\"boxShadow\":\"0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 p-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-14 h-14 rounded-full overflow-hidden flex-shrink-0 bg-surface-3\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6b\",null,{\"src\":\"https://akmweb.youngjoygame.com/web/svnres/img/test/homepage_2_2_16_1232_1/100_117b5cdcc13232157075ce7b7f6177e9.png\",\"alt\":\"Sun - Monkey King\",\"unoptimized\":false,\"priority\":\"$undefined\",\"fetchPriority\":\"$undefined\",\"fill\":true,\"className\":\"object-cover group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300\",\"sizes\":\"56px\",\"placeholder\":\"blur\",\"blurDataURL\":\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjEwMCIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj48c